      "id": 1,
      "text": "Calico Rock earned its name from a colorful rock formation that early pioneers and fur traders compared to the stripes of calico cloth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico_Rock%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "From a steamboat landing on the White River, Calico Rock grew into a railroad boomtown that fueled timber, mining, and trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explorecalico.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Perched on the north bank of the White River in the Ozark foothills, Calico Rock offers scenic bluffs and river views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico_Rock%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Calico Rock is renowned for world‑class trout fishing on the White River, drawing anglers who seek rainbow trout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
